  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 61 of the laws of 2002 amending the education law and\na chapter of the laws of 2002 amending the education law relating to requiring\ncertain public school facilities to retain on premises at least one functional\ncardiac automated external defibrillator, as proposed in legislative bill\nnumber A. 8779-A, relating to on-site cardiac automated external\ndefibrillator, in relation to naming such act the \"Louis Acompora AED's in\nschools act\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S8124",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8124-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1-a, Chap 61 of 2002",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8124\n\nSPONSOR: MARCELLINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 61 of the laws of 2002 amend-\ning the education law and a chapter of the laws of 2002 amending the\neducation law relating to requiring certain public school facilities to\nretain on premises at least one functional cardiac automated external\ndefibrillator, as proposed in legislative bill number A. 8779-A, relat-\ning to on-site cardiac automated external defibrillator, in relation to\nnaming such act the \"Louis Acompora AED's in schools act\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo name chapter 61 of the laws of 2002 the \"Louis Acompora AED's in\nSchools Act.\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends chapter 61 of the laws of 2002 by adding a new section\n1-a to name the act as the \"Louis Acompora AED's in Schools Act.\"\n\nSection 2 gives effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOn March 25, 2000, Louis J. Acompora died from sudden cardiac arrest\nafter suffering a blow to chest while playing lacrosse during his first\nhigh school game. Following Louis' tragic death, the Louis J.  Acompora\nMemorial Foundation was founded to ensure that similar tragedies are\nprevented. The Foundation has dedicated its mission to raising awareness\namong schools and other public institutions about the importance of\nowning automated external defibrillators (AED), a device which would\nhave saved Louis' life.\n\nIn 2002, New York State enacted Chapter 61, which required public school\nfacilities to provide and maintain an automated external defibrillator\n(AED). This bill would name that act the \"Louis Acompora AED's in\nSchools Act.\"\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2002:S.6851 Chapter 61\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
